 reject these flawed frameworks in favor of open-testing environments that incentivize verifiable safety through performance-based competition. Legislators should prioritize frameworks that reward modular, transparent, and resilient architectures rather than those that mandate a central, slow-moving point of failure. We do not need more gatekeepers; we need higher-velocity verification standards that match the speed of the systems we seek to field.",
